Buffer overflow 

Buffer overflow = writing more data than allocated memory
👉 strcpy causes overflow
👉 strncpy prevents overflow but can break string termination


✅ strcpy strcpy(dest, src);

👉 “Copy everything blindly until end” ❌

✅ strncpy strncpy(dest, src, n);
👉 “Copy at most N bytes, may forget to add end” ⚠️


⚠️ Hidden Risk
Even without overflow:
👉 Missing \0 causes:

Garbage printing
Reading beyond buffer
Logical errors
